 kit workspaces - lists, shows, and edits your workspaces, and says which one kit starts on

   one of
   *kit workspaces*            lists, shows, and edits your workspaces, and says which one kit starts
                             on

     --text   --json   --jq  prints as text, even on a terminal

   --show                    shows a workspace's members, each with its checkout
   --current                 says which workspace kit starts on here, and why; under kit
                             --workspace=<workspace>, the kit option before the verb, that one in
                             place of where kit runs, none naming no workspace, and an absolute path
                             the repository whose working tree holds it
   --use                     remembers a group as the last used, which kit starts on outside a
                             repository; given a <folder>, keeps the repository whose working tree
                             holds it first among the recent ones, by its desk, a linked worktree's
                             its repository's, ten at most, which the workspace menu offers
   --new                     makes a group, with the repositories given as its members
   --add <repository>
   --add --from <repository>
   --remove                  takes the repositories out of a group's members
   --rename                  gives a group a new name, in its place in the file, and keeps it the
                             last used if it was
   --delete                  takes a group, and its favorite, out of the file, and forgets it as the
                             last used; its checkouts are as they were
   --favorite                adds a workspace to the favorites
   --unfavorite              takes a workspace out of the favorites


 kit workspaces
